        "original_id": "993c9bbe-cb3f-5633-bb15-22cb8fc6acdd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Egon Schiele, Walburga \"Wally\" Neuzil, Gustav Klimt\n- Works: Portrait of Wally\n- Topics: Austrian painting, figurative painting, self-portraits\n\nFacts:\n- Egon Schiele was born on 12 June 1890 and died on 31 October 1918, and he was an Austrian painter.\n- Egon Schiele was a protégé of Gustav Klimt.\n- Egon Schiele became a major figurative painter of the early 20th century.\n- Egon Schiele's work is noted for its intensity, its raw sexuality, and the many self-portraits he produced, including naked self-portraits.\n- Egon Schiele met Walburga \"Wally\" Neuzil in 1911, when he was 21 and she was 17.\n- Portrait of Wally is a 1912 oil painting by Egon Schiele of Walburga \"Wally\" Neuzil.",
